  "note": "Municipal elections, May 1958. There was no contest after withdrawals: the ten rival Nationalist candidates for the seven West Ward seats settled, and three withdrew, leaving the new council 14 Unionists and seven Nationalists (Irish News, 8 May 1958, p. 6; Irish News, 9 May 1958, p. 1). Three of the twelve Nationalist nominees (James O'Neill, Brian Morrison and Michael McCoey) withdrew, leaving seven for seven seats. Mrs. Corrigan was the first woman member of the council. Returned unopposed."
